# A.R.I.D. Mobile Offline-First Rules

The Flutter app is an offline-first field tool. Firebase is a sync target, never a runtime dependency.

1. No screen or feature may show a loading spinner waiting on network for anything the user has already generated locally (their own reports, points, map markers).
2. All writes: **local DB first**, then the sync service (Cloudinary for photos, Firestore for metadata) — never call cloud APIs from UI code.
3. The app must be fully demoable in Airplane Mode end-to-end except for the initial map tile download.
4. Every `Report` needs a client-generated UUID before it touches the network, to make sync idempotent.
5. Points/rewards must feel instant to the user — never gate the reward feedback on a network round trip.
6. Risk colors (red/yellow/green) are only for risk-level indicators. Never use them for generic buttons or navigation.
7. Do not jump to Firebase sync work until the offline core (capture, classify, GPS, map, history, rewards) remains solid.
8. Theme colors live in `AppColors` / `AppTheme`. Do not hardcode hex values in widgets.
9. The mobile app never writes `reviewStatus` — that field belongs to the web dashboard only.
10. Do not use Firebase Storage. Report images sync through Cloudinary's free unsigned upload preset.
